## ✅ O que o site tem:

| Recurso | Descrição |
|---|---|
| 📝 Campo de texto | Para digitar anotações |
| 🏷️ Campo de título | Opcional para cada nota |
| 💾 Salvar | Guarda no `localStorage` |
| 📋 Copiar | Copia o texto para a área de transferência |
| 🗑️ Limpar/Excluir | Limpa os campos ou exclui notas |
| 🔢 Contador | Mostra quantos caracteres foram digitados |
| 💾 Persistência | As notas ficam salvas mesmo fechando o navegador |

> Basta copiar e salvar como **`anotacoes.html`** e abrir no navegador! 🚀

# C# Web Server - Hello World

Here's a simple HTTP web server using `HttpListener` that serves HTML on the `/index` endpoint.

## Code

```csharp
using System;
using System.Net;
using System.Text;
using System.Threading;
using System.Threading.Tasks;

class WebServer
{
    private static HttpListener _listener;
    private static readonly string _url = "http://localhost:8080/";
    private static CancellationTokenSource _cancellationTokenSource;

    static async Task Main(string[] args)
    {
        _cancellationTokenSource = new CancellationTokenSource();

        // Handle Ctrl+C graceful shutdown
        Console.CancelKeyPress += (sender, e) =>
        {
            e.Cancel = true;
            Console.WriteLine("\nShutting down server...");
            _cancellationTokenSource.Cancel();
        };

        await StartServer(_cancellationTokenSource.Token);
    }

    static async Task StartServer(CancellationToken cancellationToken)
    {
        _listener = new HttpListener();
        _listener.Prefixes.Add(_url);
        _listener.Start();

        Console.WriteLine("=================================");
        Console.WriteLine("  Web Server Started!");
        Console.WriteLine($"  Listening on: {_url}");
        Console.WriteLine($"  Visit: {_url}index");
        Console.WriteLine("  Press Ctrl+C to stop");
        Console.WriteLine("=================================\n");

        try
        {
            while (!cancellationToken.IsCancellationRequested)
            {
                // Wait for an incoming request
                HttpListenerContext context = await _listener.GetContextAsync()
                    .WaitAsync(cancellationToken);

                // Handle each request in a separate task
                _ = Task.Run(() => HandleRequest(context), cancellationToken);
            }
        }
        catch (OperationCanceledException)
        {
            Console.WriteLine("Server stopped.");
        }
        catch (Exception ex)
        {
            Console.WriteLine($"Server error: {ex.Message}");
        }
        finally
        {
            _listener.Stop();
            _listener.Close();
        }
    }

    static void HandleRequest(HttpListenerContext context)
    {
        HttpListenerRequest request = context.Request;
        HttpListenerResponse response = context.Response;

        string path = request.Url?.AbsolutePath ?? "/";
        string method = request.HttpMethod;

        Console.WriteLine($"[{DateTime.Now:HH:mm:ss}] {method} {path}");

        try
        {
            string responseBody;
            int statusCode;

            switch (path)
            {
                case "/index":
                case "/index.html":
                    responseBody = GetHelloWorldHtml();
                    statusCode = 200;
                    response.ContentType = "text/html; charset=utf-8";
                    break;

                case "/":
                    // Redirect root to /index
                    response.StatusCode = 301;
                    response.RedirectLocation = "/index";
                    response.Close();
                    return;

                default:
                    responseBody = Get404Html(path);
                    statusCode = 404;
                    response.ContentType = "text/html; charset=utf-8";
                    break;
            }

            byte[] buffer = Encoding.UTF8.GetBytes(responseBody);

            response.StatusCode = statusCode;
            response.ContentLength64 = buffer.Length;
            response.OutputStream.Write(buffer, 0, buffer.Length);
        }
        catch (Exception ex)
        {
            Console.WriteLine($"Request handling error: {ex.Message}");
        }
        finally
        {
            response.OutputStream.Close();
            response.Close();
        }
    }

    static string GetHelloWorldHtml()
    {
        return """
        <!DOCTYPE html>
        <html lang="en">
        <head>
            <meta charset="UTF-8">
            <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
            <title>Hello World</title>
            <style>
                * {
                    margin: 0;
                    padding: 0;
                    box-sizing: border-box;
                }

                body {
                    font-family: 'Segoe UI', Tahoma, Geneva, Verdana, sans-serif;
                    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #667eea 0%, #764ba2 100%);
                    min-height: 100vh;
                    display: flex;
                    justify-content: center;
                    align-items: center;
                }

                .container {
                    text-align: center;
                    background: white;
                    padding: 60px 80px;
                    border-radius: 16px;
                    box-shadow: 0 20px 60px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);
                }

                h1 {
                    font-size: 3rem;
                    color: #333;
                    margin-bottom: 16px;
                }

                p {
                    font-size: 1.2rem;
                    color: #666;
                    margin-bottom: 8px;
                }

                .badge {
                    display: inline-block;
                    margin-top: 20px;
                    padding: 8px 20px;
                    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #667eea, #764ba2);
                    color: white;
                    border-radius: 20px;
                    font-size: 0.9rem;
                    font-weight: bold;
                }
            </style>
        </head>
        <body>
            <div class="container">
                <h1>Hello, World! 👋</h1>
                <p>Welcome to my C# Web Server</p>
                <p>Built with HttpListener</p>
                <div class="badge">Running on .NET</div>
            </div>
        </body>
        </html>
        """;
    }

    static string Get404Html(string path)
    {
        return $"""
        <!DOCTYPE html>
        <html lang="en">
        <head>
            <meta charset="UTF-8">
            <title>404 - Not Found</title>
            <style>
                body {{
                    font-family: 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;
                    background: #1a1a2e;
                    color: white;
                    display: flex;
                    justify-content: center;
                    align-items: center;
                    min-height: 100vh;
                    margin: 0;
                    text-align: center;
                }}
                h1 {{ font-size: 5rem; color: #e94560; margin-bottom: 10px; }}
                p {{ color: #aaa; font-size: 1.1rem; }}
                a {{ color: #667eea; text-decoration: none; }}
                a:hover {{ text-decoration: underline; }}
            </style>
        </head>
        <body>
            <div>
                <h1>404</h1>
                <p>The path <strong>{path}</strong> was not found.</p>
                <p><a href="/index">← Go back to Home</a></p>
            </div>
        </body>
        </html>
        """;
    }
}
```

## Project Setup

Create a new console project and run it:

```bash
dotnet new console -n HelloWorldServer
cd HelloWorldServer
# Replace Program.cs with the code above
dotnet run
```

## Features

| Feature | Description |
|---|---|
| `/index` | Serves Hello World HTML page |
| `/` | Redirects to `/index` |
| Any other path | Returns a styled 404 page |
| Concurrency | Each request handled in its own Task |
| Graceful shutdown | `Ctrl+C` stops the server cleanly |
| Request logging | Logs method, path, and timestamp to console |

## Notes

> **Windows Admin**: If you get an `Access Denied` error on Windows, either run as Administrator or register the URL:
> ```bash
> netsh http add urlacl url=http://localhost:8080/ user=YOUR_USERNAME
> ```

Once running, visit **http://localhost:8080/index** in your browser.

