# Chrome Extension: Auto-Highlight Element

I'll create a complete Chrome extension that automatically finds and highlights elements with the specified class.

## File Structure
```
highlight-extension/
├── manifest.json
├── content.js
├── popup.html
├── popup.js
└── icons/
    └── icon48.png (optional)
```

---

## manifest.json

```json
{
  "manifest_version": 3,
  "name": "Element Highlighter",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "description": "Auto-highlights elements with v-card__text headline text-center px-0 class in red",
  "permissions": [
    "activeTab",
    "scripting",
    "storage"
  ],
  "host_permissions": [
    "<all_urls>"
  ],
  "content_scripts": [
    {
      "matches": ["<all_urls>"],
      "js": ["content.js"],
      "run_at": "document_idle"
    }
  ],
  "action": {
    "default_popup": "popup.html",
    "default_title": "Element Highlighter",
    "default_icon": {
      "48": "icons/icon48.png"
    }
  }
}
```

